      "name": "mount",
      "optional": false,
      "docstring": "Mount type of the antenna. Reserved keywords include: ”EQUATORIAL” - equatorial mount;\n”ALT-AZ”: azimuth-elevation mount;\n\"ALT-AZ+ROTATOR\": alt-az mount with feed rotator; introduced for ASKAP dishes;\n\"ALT-AZ+NASMYTH-R\": Nasmyth mount with receivers at the right-hand side of the cabin. Many high-frequency antennas used for VLBI have such a mount typel;\n\"ALT-AZ+NASMYTH-L\": Nasmyth mount with receivers at the left-hand side of the cabin.\n\"ALT-AZ+BWG-R\": alt-az mount that uses a Beam Wave Guide to bring the focus down to the pedestal. The receivers are at the right-hand side of the cabin (-R). Compared to the Nasmyth mounts there is an extra correction term because there are now two rotating mirrors. See https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.13381 for more details.\n\"ALT-AZ+BWG-L\": alt-az mount that uses a Beam Wave Guide, as above, but with receivers at the left-hand side of the cabin.\n”X-Y”: x-y mount;\n”SPACE-HALCA” - specific orientation model."
    },
    {
      "$class": "ArraySchemaRef",
      "schema_name": null,
      "dimensions": [
        [
          "antenna_name"
        ]
      ],
      "dtypes": [
        "<U0"
      ],
      "coordinates": [],
      "attributes": [],
      "class_docstring": null,
      "data_docstring": null,
      "name": "telescope_name",
      "optional": false,
      "docstring": "Useful when data is combined from mutiple arrays for example ACA + ALMA. "
    },
